{"op": "replace", "segment": 18, "fixes": "S-019", "text": "Confidential Information includes verbally conveyed information, including information shared in meetings, calls or demonstrations, whether or not it is written down or marked."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 23, "fixes": "S-020", "text": "Receiving Party may share some Confidential Information with some of Receiving Party's employees, provided that such employees are bound by obligations of confidentiality at least as restrictive as these terms and conditions. Receiving Party's employees who need the information for their work must be permitted to see it."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 24, "fixes": "S-024", "text": "Recipient shall not without Disclosing Party’s prior written consent reverse engineer, disassemble or decompile any prototypes, software or other objects which embody the Disclosing Party’s Confidential Information for any purpose, and to the extent such consent is granted Recipient shall receive and hold such Confidential Information subject to the terms of this Agreement."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 34, "fixes": "S-021", "text": "5.1. is already known or in the possession of Recipient or its Affiliate at the time of disclosure as shown by contemporaneous written records of Recipient or its Affiliate, which Recipient shall provide to Disclosing Party on request and which Recipient bears the burden of proving, otherwise than as a result of any improper act or omission of Recipient or its Affiliate; or"},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 49, "fixes": "S-023", "text": "If Recipient is compelled by law, regulation, court order or other governmental process to disclose any Confidential Information, or else be liable for contempt or other penalty, Recipient may disclose such Confidential Information without liability under this Agreement, provided that Recipient first gives Disclosing Party prompt written notice so that Disclosing Party may seek a protective order or other remedy, and discloses only the portion legally required."}
]}

