{"op": "replace", "segment": 6, "fixes": "S-020", "text": "3. The Recipient undertakes to keep the Confidential Information secure and not to disclose it to any third party, except that the Recipient may share it with its employees who need it for their work and with its advisers, auditors and subcontractors who need it and are bound by written confidentiality obligations no less protective than this Agreement, provided that the Recipient identifies such advisers, auditors and subcontractors to the Discloser on request and remains responsible for any breach by them."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 13, "fixes": "S-021", "text": "8. The undertakings in clauses 2 and 3 will continue in force for sixty (60) months, and such undertakings survive the end of this Agreement for that period. After that period, the Recipient shall not use or disclose any Confidential Information that remains sensitive or confidential without the Discloser’s prior written consent."},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 16, "fixes": "S-019", "text": "The Receiving Party may develop, acquire or market products or services similar to those of the Disclosing Party, provided that it does not use the Confidential Information in doing so. Nothing herein restricts the Receiving Party from obtaining similar information lawfully from an independent third party, provided that the Receiving Party can show by contemporaneous written records that such information was obtained without use of or reference to the Confidential Information."}
